menu "PluTO motion profile"

    comment "Starting points: tune them on the bench with the antenna mounted."
    comment "Compile-time constants, unlike the NVS seeds: change, rebuild, flash."

    config PLUTO_MOTION_MAX_SPEED_DEG_S
        int "Top speed of each servo axis (degrees per second)"
        default 60
        range 1 600
        help
            The fastest either axis is commanded to move (HU-36). Lower is gentler on the gears and the mount, but the pan
            follows the azimuth, which turns at about 25 deg/s at the top of a
            pass culminating at 88 degrees. Below about 20 the pan falls behind
            there: test_a_high_pass_keeps_up in components/rotor/test_host
            misses by 0.3 degrees at 20, 1.1 at 15 and 3.1 at 10, against 0.07
            at this default. A flip swings the pan 180 degrees, which takes
            about 3.5 s at 60.

    config PLUTO_MOTION_MAX_ACCEL_DEG_S2
        int "Top acceleration of each servo axis (degrees per second squared)"
        default 120
        range 1 5000
        help
            The fastest either axis speeds up or slows down, including the
            braking after a HOLD (HU-36). This is what spares the gears the jerk
            of a servo told to jump: at 120 an axis reaches 60 deg/s in half a
            second and stops from it within 15 degrees. Too low and high passes
            fall behind as well: the same test misses by 0.3 degrees at 30.

    config PLUTO_MOTION_REST_AFTER_MS
        int "Time still before the servo outputs can be released (ms)"
        default 5000
        range 0 3600000
        help
            Once both axes have stood still at the same target for this long,
            the rotor task releases both servo outputs, and a new target brings
            them back before the first move (HU-35). 0 never releases them. Whether
            a DS3218 without pulses holds its position or sags under the
            antenna is still to be measured on the bench; if the tilt sags,
            lengthen this so it only acts between passes, or set it to 0.

endmenu
